From: postmarketOS polaris fix <local@localhost>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dsi/phy: power up the digital top before starting
 the 10nm PLL

dsi_pll_10nm_vco_prepare() only sets CMN_CTRL_0 BIT(5) (PLL bias) via
dsi_pll_enable_pll_bias(), but leaves the PHY digital top powered down
(BIT(6) clear).  Since the clock framework can enable the PLL early at
probe time (via assigned-clock-parents in qcom dispcc), before the PHY
driver's dsi_10nm_phy_enable() runs, the PLL cannot lock and
dsi_pll_10nm_lock_status() reads back COMMON_STATUS_ONE == 0x00000000:

  msm_dsi_phy ae94400.phy: [drm:dsi_pll_10nm_vco_prepare] *ERROR* DSI PLL(0) lock failed, status=0x00000000
  panel-jdi-nt35596s ae94000.dsi.0: failed to send DCS Init 1st Code: -22

This mirrors the 7nm fix from Dmitry Baryshkov
("drm/msm/dsi/phy: power up the digital top before starting the 7nm PLL")
and Luca Weiss confirmed the same fix applies to the 10nm PHY.

Power up the digital top together with the PLL bias, and clear both bits
on disable.

Tested on Xiaomi Mi MIX 2S (polaris, SDM845): DSI PLL locks, panel
receives DCS init, display outputs.

Signed-off-by: polaris port <local@localhost>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy_10nm.c | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy_10nm.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy_10nm.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy_10nm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy_10nm.c
@@ -303,7 +303,7 @@ static void dsi_pll_disable_pll_bias(struct dsi_pll_10nm *pll)
 	u32 data = readl(pll->phy->base + REG_DSI_10nm_PHY_CMN_CTRL_0);
 
 	writel(0, pll->phy->pll_base + REG_DSI_10nm_PHY_PLL_SYSTEM_MUXES);
-	writel(data & ~BIT(5), pll->phy->base + REG_DSI_10nm_PHY_CMN_CTRL_0);
+	writel(data & ~(BIT(6) | BIT(5)), pll->phy->base + REG_DSI_10nm_PHY_CMN_CTRL_0);
 	ndelay(250);
 }
 
@@ -311,7 +311,7 @@ static void dsi_pll_enable_pll_bias(struct dsi_pll_10nm *pll)
 {
 	u32 data = readl(pll->phy->base + REG_DSI_10nm_PHY_CMN_CTRL_0);
 
-	writel(data | BIT(5), pll->phy->base + REG_DSI_10nm_PHY_CMN_CTRL_0);
+	writel(data | BIT(6) | BIT(5), pll->phy->base + REG_DSI_10nm_PHY_CMN_CTRL_0);
 	writel(0xc0, pll->phy->pll_base + REG_DSI_10nm_PHY_PLL_SYSTEM_MUXES);
 	ndelay(250);
 }
